    <bib:Article rdf:about="#item_196">
        <z:itemType>journalArticle</z:itemType>
        <dcterms:isPartOf>
            <bib:Journal>
                <prism:volume>14</prism:volume>
                <dc:title>Education Sciences</dc:title>
                <dc:identifier>DOI 10.3390/educsci14050530</dc:identifier>
                <prism:number>5</prism:number>
            </bib:Journal>
        </dcterms:isPartOf>
        <bib:authors>
            <rdf:Seq>
                <rdf:li>
                    <foaf:Person>
                       <foaf:surname>Kinderberg, Björn</foaf:surname>
                    </foaf:Person>
                </rdf:li>
            </rdf:Seq>
        </bib:authors>
        <dcterms:isReferencedBy rdf:resource="#item_205"/>
        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_197"/>
        <dc:title>ChatGPT-Generated and Student-Written Historical Narratives: A Comparative Analysis</dc:title>
        <dc:date>2024</dc:date>
        <bib:pages>530</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_205">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;ChatGPT Excels in Narrative Quality but Lacks Emotional and Moral Dimensions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location: Pages 7–9, &quot;Results&quot; section, particularly Figures 1, 2, and corresponding analysis&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;Evaluation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;The study clearly shows that ChatGPT outperforms student writing in terms of linguistic fluency, structural coherence, and the use of complex rhetorical devices. However, it is notably weak in &quot;moral response stance&quot; and &quot;emotional expression.&quot; Especially without feedback, its texts appear detached, analytical, and lack human warmth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;Proposes a Constructive Shift: From &quot;Preventing Plagiarism&quot; to &quot;Guided Utilization&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location: Latter part of Page 14, &quot;Discussion&quot; section&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;Evaluation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(15, 17, 21)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Instead of merely criticizing, the authors offer forward-looking pedagogical recommendations: rather than attempting to eliminate the use of ChatGPT, it should be leveraged as a teaching aid—for generating writing templates, providing feedback, simulating historical perspectives, etc.—thereby integrating AI into a &quot;coaching-style&quot; teaching process to empower rather than replace student learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
    <z:Attachment rdf:about="#item_197">
